WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.997
<v Examiner>Glaucoma and cataracts.

2
00:00:02.997 --> 00:00:03.757
<v Examiner>Four marks.

3
00:00:04.207 --> 00:00:09.394
<v Examiner>Explain glaucoma and cataracts: which part of the eye each one affects, what goes wrong,

4
00:00:09.394 --> 00:00:10.927
<v Examiner>and how it affects vision.

5
00:00:11.377 --> 00:00:15.712
Another one from her help board, and she sums them up in a few words each.

6
00:00:15.712 --> 00:00:17.705
Glaucoma: the pressure in the eye.

7
00:00:17.705 --> 00:00:19.697
Cataract: the clarity of the lens.

8
00:00:20.147 --> 00:00:24.302
The hook: glaucoma is a pressure problem, because the drain blocks.

9
00:00:24.302 --> 00:00:28.147
A cataract is a clarity problem, because the lens goes cloudy.

10
00:00:28.597 --> 00:00:29.549
Glaucoma first.

11
00:00:29.549 --> 00:00:34.185
It involves the aqueous humour, the watery fluid at the front of the eye.

12
00:00:34.185 --> 00:00:39.773
Normally the ciliary body makes it and the canal of Schlemm drains it, at the same rate.

13
00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:43.711
If the canal of Schlemm is blocked, or too much fluid is made,

14
00:00:43.711 --> 00:00:49.109
aqueous humour builds up in the anterior segment, and the intraocular pressure rises.

15
00:00:49.109 --> 00:00:54.570
That pressure compresses the retina and its blood supply, and damages the optic nerve.

16
00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.555
So vision is lost, and it can end in blindness.

17
00:00:59.005 --> 00:01:00.115
Now the cataract.

18
00:01:00.115 --> 00:01:01.943
A cataract affects the lens.

19
00:01:01.943 --> 00:01:07.753
The proteins in the lens denature, so the lens turns cloudy, or opaque, instead of clear.

20
00:01:07.753 --> 00:01:11.475
The cloudy lens stops light reaching the retina properly,

21
00:01:11.475 --> 00:01:17.220
so vision becomes blurred and yellowed, with poor night vision and sensitivity to glare.

22
00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.766
It's common with age and with diabetes.

23
00:01:19.766 --> 00:01:23.227
And it's treated with surgery that replaces the lens.

24
00:01:24.677 --> 00:01:25.333
The traps.

25
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:26.382
Don't swap them.

26
00:01:26.382 --> 00:01:30.711
Glaucoma is pressure: the aqueous humour and the canal of Schlemm.

27
00:01:30.711 --> 00:01:32.220
A cataract is the lens.

28
00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:37.271
Second: the ciliary body makes the fluid, and the canal of Schlemm drains it.

29
00:01:37.271 --> 00:01:39.632
Third: in glaucoma the lens is fine.

30
00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:43.109
It's the retina and the optic nerve that get damaged.

31
00:01:43.559 --> 00:01:44.160
<v Examiner>Once more.

32
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.543
<v Examiner>Glaucoma and cataracts.

33
00:01:47.993 --> 00:01:53.801
Glaucoma: aqueous humour is made by the ciliary body and drained by the canal of Schlemm.

34
00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:58.305
If the drain blocks, fluid builds up, the intraocular pressure rises,

35
00:01:58.305 --> 00:02:03.135
and it damages the retina and the optic nerve, which can end in blindness.

36
00:02:03.135 --> 00:02:07.377
A cataract: the proteins of the lens denature, so it goes cloudy.

37
00:02:07.377 --> 00:02:10.510
Vision becomes blurred and yellowed, with glare.

38
00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:13.708
It's treated with surgery that replaces the lens.
